## 7. Security tools

The repository framework may also use security tools as part of its CI pipeline.

| Tool | Primary purpose |
|---|---|
| CodeQL | Static code analysis to identify potential security vulnerabilities |
| Black Duck | Software composition analysis, including open-source and third-party dependency risks |
| Veracode | Application security testing, depending on the products and scan types configured |

These tools complement Ruff and pytest.

- Ruff focuses on code quality and certain coding problems.
- Pytest checks application behavior.
- CodeQL identifies potential security issues in code.
- Black Duck analyzes software components and dependencies.
- Veracode performs configured application security scans.

The exact checks depend on each tool's configuration and the workflow.

